# Cursor Rules for Portfolio Project

## Function Declarations
- Always prefer `function functionName() {}` notation over `const functionName = () => {}` or `const functionName = function() {}`
- Only use `const` for functions when:
  - The function needs to be reassigned
  - The function is part of an object literal or class method
  - The function is passed as a callback and arrow function syntax is more appropriate for `this` binding
- For standalone functions, always use `function` keyword declaration

## Code Style
- Use consistent formatting and naming conventions
- Prefer explicit over implicit
- Keep functions focused and single-purpose

